# Program kind

With `kind: Program` you write a `Main` method plus any fields, helper methods and
types it needs. Invoklet supplies the surrounding class and calls `Main` for you.

```csharp run
void Main()
{
    var inventory = new Inventory();
    inventory.Add("Keyboard", 3);
    inventory.Add("Mouse", 5);
    inventory.Add("Keyboard", 2);

    inventory.Lines().Dump("Inventory");
    Console.WriteLine($"Total items: {Total(inventory)}");
}

static int Total(Inventory inventory) => inventory.Lines().Sum(line => line.Quantity);

class Inventory
{
    private readonly Dictionary<string, int> _counts = new();

    public void Add(string name, int quantity) =>
        _counts[name] = _counts.GetValueOrDefault(name) + quantity;

    public IEnumerable<StockLine> Lines() =>
        _counts.OrderBy(pair => pair.Key).Select(pair => new StockLine(pair.Key, pair.Value));
}

record StockLine(string Name, int Quantity);
```
